    "crc_mean_set_size": 4.6116838487972505,
    "delta_mean_set_size": 0.0,
    "agree": true,
    "note": "Both formalisms return the same FAMILY of rule -- include every sentence whose normalised score clears a cut -- and differ only in how the cut is chosen: LAC takes the ceil((n+1)(1-alpha)) quantile of the gold sentence's non-conformity, conformal risk control takes the largest cut whose finite-sample risk bound still clears alpha. So this is a cross-check on the CALIBRATION step, not on the prediction rule, and it is worth stating that way rather than claiming more. What it establishes is that the coverage statement does not depend on which of the two the examiner prefers -- which matters here because no named theorem covers LAC over instance-dependent label spaces, while conformal risk control never assumes a shared label space at all. `cuts_coincide` says whether the two landed on the same cut to the grid resolution."
  },
